<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Nov forex reserves up at $1.344 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Nov forex reserves up at $1.344 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves rose to $1.344 billion in November from $1.262 billion in October, but lower compared to $1.832 billion in November 1995, the State Bank of Pakistan said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The central bank gave no reason for the rise.</p>
<p>The reserves included $425 million within Pakistan and $241 million outside Pakistan, the bank said.</p>
<p>Following is the monthly foreign exchange reserves holdings position in Pakistan:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		NOV	  OCT	  NOV 95</p>
<p> TOTAL			 1,344	1,262	 1,832</p>
<p> Forex in Pakistan	   425	  543	   841</p>
<p> Forex outside Pakistan    241	   30	   283</p>
<p> Gold coins and bullion    676	  676	   707</p>
<p> Special Drawing Rights	2	   13	     1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
